      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1808 Concord became New Hampshire's state capital, and the State House was finished in 1819, the oldest state capitol building still in use.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Concord%2C_New_Hampshire",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city sits on the Merrimack River, where granite quarrying once supplied stone for the Library of Congress in Washington, D.C.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2",
